2026-08-16T15:43:24Z    [HD:Net sales] GATE critic: You rolled FY2026Q2 off FY2025Q2 by reusing the FY2024Q2→FY2025Q2 growth split (+1.0% comparable +3.861% non‑comparable), i.e., 45,300 × (1 + 0.01 + 0.03861) = 47,502.2 USDm. That 3.861% “non‑comparable” piece is a one‑time YoY bridge specific to FY2025 (store adds/acquisition/calendar) and is already embedded in the FY2025Q2 base; applying it again to FY2026Q2 double‑counts it. This is a wrong-basis error that likely overstates the forecast.
2026-08-16T15:43:25Z    [DE:Worldwide net sales and revenues] GATE critic: Your trend input misstates the prior-year YoY change: Deere’s own release says “Worldwide net sales and revenues decreased 9 percent, to $12.018 billion, for the third quarter of 2025.” You use -8.6% for FY2024Q3→FY2025Q3, which contradicts the reported -9%. Since your -11.68% projection is built from that mis-stated YoY, the resulting 10,614.8 USDm is on the wrong basis.
